-- Hide two landmarks, at every zoom level.
--
-- Overviews are built by averaging the level below, so the pixels over a
-- withheld location are present in every coarser tile as well. Withholding it
-- only at full resolution leaves it legible at 1 m, at 2 m, and so on up --
-- which is what `hide-landmarks-high-detail.cql2` does, deliberately. This is
-- the version that actually hides the location.
--
-- It costs the overviews. Withholding a tile at level 5 -- one tile, covering
-- the whole image -- takes the entire zoomed-out view with it. At the levels
-- in between the loss is proportionate: 2 tiles of 12 at level 3, so the city
-- is readable with two dark patches in it.
--
-- There is no third option at tile granularity. Either the location survives
-- in the overviews, or the overviews lose ground around it. Choosing means
-- deciding which you can live with, and the two files here are the two
-- choices written out.
--
-- Withheld on data/paris-landmarks.tif: 21 tiles, 386,862 bytes.

region.kind = 'metadata'

OR (region.kind = 'tile'
    AND NOT S_INTERSECTS(region.geom, POLYGON((
      255320 6250770, 255525 6250770, 255525 6250975, 255320 6250975, 255320 6250770)))
    AND NOT S_INTERSECTS(region.geom, POLYGON((
      255350 6253350, 255610 6253350, 255610 6253600, 255350 6253600, 255350 6253350))))
